// Each declaration here is refused at its carrier.
//
// A head takes only its own implicit `A`, so a supply of another name is an
// error. An omitted carrier needs an endpoint that fixes it.
//
// Each head refuses a supply of `B` as `UnresolvedName` at `B`. A flow
// between two lambdas refuses as `ImplicitUnsolved`, since a lambda
// synthesises no type.
//
// - see: `../../model/identity/carrier-by-name.gandr` — the carriers admitted
// - see: #4932

/// `Path`'s carrier is the implicit `A`, and no implicit `B`.
@[ refuses("UnresolvedName") ]
def strayPath : Path[.B = Integer](4, 4) = Path.here(4);

/// `Bridge`'s carrier is the implicit `A`, and no implicit `B`.
@[ refuses("UnresolvedName") ]
def strayBridge : Bridge[.B = Integer](4, 4) = unit;

/// `Flow`'s carrier is the implicit `A`, and no implicit `B`.
@[ refuses("UnresolvedName") ]
def strayFlow : Flow[.B = Integer](4, 4) = Flow.stay(4);

/// Two lambdas synthesise no type, so nothing fixes the omitted carrier.
@[ refuses("ImplicitUnsolved") ]
def unfixedFlow : Flow(fun (y) { y }, fun (y) { y }) = Flow.stay(fun (y) { y });
